+# M9: Requested changes before go-live (G-31)
+
+Requested by the developer for the client on 14 October 2026 and approved in writing (spec §20.3). Spec update 7.
+
+## T9.1 Starter-kit leftovers and log safety
+
+**Goal:** nothing on screen points to another site, and nothing a user sees is written to the log.
+
+**Build exactly:** delete the unused starter-kit files `components/app-header.tsx` (links to GitHub and laravel.com), `layouts/app/app-header-layout.tsx`, `components/nav-footer.tsx`, `components/text-link.tsx`. `WarningRequired` and `ConcurrentEdit` in `dontReport` (BR-SEC-17: a duplicate-party message holds a party name). Inertia DevTools (`config/inertia.php`) off unless `INERTIA_DEVTOOLS_ENABLED=true` with `APP_ENV=local`. Developer guide notes.
+
+**Tests:** `ProtectedAppTest` (no warning or concurrent edit reported; DevTools off and local-only; no link to another site in `resources/js` or `resources/views`).
+
+**Done when:** tests pass.
+
+---
+
+## T9.2 Speed
+
+**Goal:** the laptop and the server answer quickly; NFR-02 holds on the developer's laptop.
+
+**Build exactly:** Inertia SSR off (servers never build an SSR bundle; with the Vite dev server it rendered every full page load through Vite). `composer run dev` runs `serve --no-reload` and `.env.example` sets `PHP_CLI_SERVER_WORKERS=4`. `Ageing::overdueMany` and `Ageing::averageDaysToPayMany`: the oldest-first figures (§12.6) for many buyers in one PostgreSQL query each (numeric; the final division in `Decimal`), used by the overdue-buyers alert, pending balances and business insights; insights supplier balances in one `partyNets()` query. `zb:time-pages` times the 3-month statement PDF. Timings before and after, on the same machine, in `docs/release-checks.md`.
+
+**Not in this task:** lazy loading of the signed-in layout (it would add a request to every signed-in first page to save 1 request on the cached login page).
+
+**Tests:** `AgeingOverdueManyTest` (newest-first rule against the existing match on 3,000 random histories; both SQL functions against `overdueFor()` and `averageDaysToPay()` on AT-2 and on a random history posted through the Actions). T-12 and AT-1 to AT-6 unchanged.
+
+**Done when:** tests pass; every page in `zb:time-pages` under 3 seconds on the measured machine, recorded.
+
+---
+
+## T9.3 Simple dashboard for the Accountant
+
+**Goal:** BR-DSH-01.
+
+**Build exactly:** permission `dashboard.balances` (Owner only) in `RolesAndPermissionsSeeder`; `DashboardController` sends and computes balances only with it; the page hides the block without it.
+
+**Tests:** `AccountantDashboardTest`; `RolesAndPermissionsTest` lists the new key.
+
+**Done when:** tests pass; screenshot at 375 px for both roles.
+
+---
+
+## T9.4 Long report ranges
+
+**Goal:** BR-RPT-09, BR-RPT-10, BR-RPT-11 (closes the four 12-month views of T8.2).
+
+**Build exactly:** `AccountStatement::for(..., $page, $perPage = 100)` with the running balance as a PostgreSQL window sum and `pages` for the shared `Pagination`; "Brought forward" on later pages. `RateWeightReports::rateMonths` and `weightMonths` (SQL per month, rate corrections included) when `Dates::longerThanThreeMonths()`; `monthly` prop and note. Statement PDF: 3-month limit and default (`Dates::threeMonthsBefore()`). Share PDF shows a refusal message instead of saving an error page.
+
+**Tests:** `AccountStatementPagesTest`; `LongRangeReportsTest`.
+
+**Done when:** tests pass.
+
+---
+
+## T9.5 Public ids in links and filters
+
+**Goal:** BR-SEC-19.
+
+**Build exactly:** migration `add_public_id_to_linked_tables` (`uuid` default `gen_random_uuid()`, unique) on the 13 tables of §9.1; trait `App\Support\HasPublicId` (route key, UUID v4 on create, `idFromPublic()` for filters, 404 for unknown); UUID route patterns for every record parameter; every prop that builds a link carries `public_id`; links built on the server use the model or its `public_id`; address-bar filters (`party_id`, `category_id`, `money_account_id`, `item_id`, `user_id`, `source_id`, `target_id`, create-page `party_id`) carry the public id. Form bodies keep internal numbers.
+
+**Tests:** `PublicIdTest` (numeric and malformed ids 404; another company's public id 404; filters by public id; links in page data use public ids). Existing tests that put internal numbers in URLs are changed only there, listed in the pull request.
+
+**Done when:** tests pass; T-09 passes over every route.
